  "findings": [
    "Inspected DiagramChromeFactory12026#create wrapper order (body, legend, title, caption, header/footer), DecorateEntityImage dimensions/centering, DrawableSet#asTextBlock/drawU22/clipAndTranslate2. The new legacy horizontal max-width calculation follows this order and default right margin5 is directly sourced. Four fresh legacy wide/narrow chrome plus cross-page activation controls pass.",
    "Focused legacy legend+title+caption disproves full TextBlock composition: Java height231 versus Rust212, caption y220.7988 versus169.3105 even with matching width404. Rust still calculates caption_top from tail boxes and takes max with legend height rather than stacking caption after the decorated legend block. The multiline version also emits34 elements instead of35 because caption measurement/paint does not create line blocks.",
    "Every Teoz page control fails. Rust still truncates the body at newpage whereas raw Java Teoz renders the combined history in these inputs (primary height437 versus324), and Teoz retains participant-midpoint chrome feedback. No helper-only width or clipping acceptance can cover these whole-page failures.",
    "All14 accounts were present byte-for-byte in earlier chronological commits before their corresponding code. See provenance.json and commit-mapping.json. Main release tiers remain11181/11251 product-library and10497/11251 assisted-library; source-only CLI cohort403/955 with10 invalid references; no regressions observed.",
    "Verdict applies to whole source-to-SVG recovery with the dependencies described above. Positive component-local observations are explicitly bounded and are not acceptance. Every mismatch and negative remains in the standing suite."
